      ],
      "source": "https://mainepedia.com/towns/milbridge/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Milbridge sits at the mouth of the 55‑mile Narraguagus River, where it empties into Narraguagus Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mainepedia.com/towns/milbridge/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Milbridge remains a working fishing village, with a lobster fleet and traditions of wild blueberry harvesting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mainepedia.com/towns/milbridge/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every July, Milbridge hosts its annual Milbridge Days Celebration, featuring a parade and the famous Codfish Relay Race.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
